<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Lycée Pétion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1816">1816</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Lycée Pétion is a secondary school in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/port-au-prince">Port-au-Prince</a>, founded in 1816 under President <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexandre-petion">Alexandre Pétion</a> and named after him. One of the oldest schools in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/haiti">Haiti</a> and long the capital's leading public secondary school, it educated much of the country's political and intellectual elite in the nineteenth and twentieth centuries.</p></div>
